{"timestamp":"2026-04-23T22:25:54.061Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The current fix is broken in a specific way.\n\n`objectsigner.go` does this:\n\n- load system config\n- load global config\n- `config.Merge(sysCfg, globalCfg)`\n- check `hasCustomSSHSignProgram(merged.Raw)`\n\nThe problem is in go-git itself. In [config.go](/Users/pfleidi/go/pkg/mod/github.com/go-git/go-git/v6@v6.0.0-alpha.2/config/config.go:227), `Merge` explicitly ignores `Raw`:\n\n```go\n// The config field Raw cannot be merged via reflection, so it is ignored\n// as part of the Merge operation. To update Raw after a merge, call Marshal().\n```\n\nThat matters because `gpg.ssh.program` is not represented in go-git’s typed config. It only exists in raw config. So after `config.Merge(...)`, `merged.Raw` no longer reliably contains `gpg.ssh.program`.\n\nThat makes this check in [objectsigner.go](/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/fix/1password-commit-signing/cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go:44) ineffective:\n\n```go\nif auto.Format(merged.GPG.Format) == auto.FormatSSH && hasCustomSSHSignProgram(merged.Raw) {\n    ...\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\nWhy this matches your symptom:\n- your repo is `local_dev: true` in `.entire/settings.json`\n- Codex hooks are using `go run \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"/cmd/entire/main.go ...`\n- the warning comes from [objectsigner.go](/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/fix/1password-commit-signing/cmd/entire/cli/objectsigner.go:59)\n- sign attempts happen on checkpoint commit creation/push paths, which is why you notice it especially with AI-agent-driven pushes\n\nYour current git config is exactly the 1Password case:\n\n- `user.signingkey = ssh-ed25519 ...`\n- `gpg.format = ssh`\n- `gpg.ssh.program = /Applications/1Password.app/Contents/MacOS/op-ssh-sign`\n- `commit.gpgsign = true`\n\nSo the intended skip should happen, but the raw field is lost before the check.\n\nPlan to fix:\n1. Read `gpg.ssh.program` from the raw per-scope configs before merging, not from `merged.Raw`.\n2. Make the skip decision from those raw scoped configs.\n3. Keep the typed merged config only for fields go-git actually models (`commit.gpgsign`, `gpg.format`, `user.signingKey`).\n4. Add a regression test that proves a raw `gpg.ssh.program` survives detection across the current code path.\n5. Run `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and `staticcheck ./...` and show output.\n\nIf you approve, I’ll implement only step 1 of that plan and stop for review.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
